🚨→⚠️ **IMPORTANT (confirm against companion runtime): `expectNonZeroExit` throw-vs-return contract is load-bearing for the gh-683/gh-1164 probe filter**

The whole `buildExclusionPathspecs` filter depends on the runtime **throwing** on a non-zero probe exit:

```javascript
try {
    runCommand({ command: 'git check-ignore -q -- ' + path, expectNonZeroExit: true });
    return false; // ignored — git's own exclude machinery owns it
} catch (e) {
    return true; // not ignored (or probe unavailable) — pathspec exclusion required
}
```

If the companion runtime support (`epam/dm.ai#790`, `epam/dmtools-dart#469`) implements `expectNonZeroExit` as "treat the non-zero exit as success and **return** normally", every `git check-ignore -q` probe on a NOT-ignored path would fall into the `return false` branch → all `:!` exclusions are dropped → `git add` names ignored-untracked paths in its pathspecs → the exact gh-683/gh-1164 ignored-pathspec guard failure returns at every staging site.

What I verified during this review on the **currently installed** DMTools 0.1.43 runtime (`grep -c -a expectNonZeroExit dmtools.bin` → 0 matches; live probe in a scratch repo):

- `cli_execute_command({ command: 'git check-ignore -q -- tracked.txt', expectNonZeroExit: true })` → **THREW** `Command execution failed (exit code 1)` — the unknown option is tolerated (no validator rejection) and the throw contract is preserved, so behavior today is byte-identical to pre-PR. Good.
- The PR description says the companion runtime "logs a single concise DEBUG line instead", which implies throw-semantics are kept — but that claim is not verifiable from this repo, and no unit test here can pin it (the runner is mocked).

Please confirm against the companion runtime PRs that `expectNonZeroExit: true` **still throws** to the JS caller (only the ERROR stack-trace logging is silenced). If confirmed, this stands as-is; if the runtime ever returns instead of throwing, this becomes blocking. Also note the noise fix stays inert in production until those runtimes are deployed — worth stating in the PR description if not obvious.

⚠️ **IMPORTANT: option-forwarding change is not pinned by any unit test at the three call sites**

The new unit test (`js/unit-tests/test_gitStaging.js:191`) pins only the gitStaging side — that the probe args carry `expectNonZeroExit: true`. The other half of the fix, the forwarding through the wrappers, is untested; reverting any of these call-site changes would not fail a single test:

- `js/common/gitOps.js:34` — `dirScopedCmd`'s new `extraOpts` merge (`Object.assign({}, cmdOpts, extraOpts || {}, { command: command })`);
